  {
   "id": 639833,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/57447e51147b508a.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work from ResearchGate)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The image shows the number of species for Asian frogs. The x-axis is time in millions of years. The top image shows main frog lineages, and the graph shows the number of frog species.</p>\n<p>Which statement best describes the speciation in this example?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1246850,
     "content_html": "This is an example of gradual speciation, happening at a near-constant rate over time."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246849,
     "content_html": "This is an example of gradual speciation with a slightly higher rate than expected."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246851,
     "content_html": "This is an example of punctuated equilibrium and the frog species are experiencing the sudden jump."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246848,
     "content_html": "This is an example of punctuated equilibrium and the frog species have stabilized after the jump."
    }
   ],
